a rich error object, which is what the last testsuite case could not build

connection_client_error_no_server was the ONE case in the whole suite that did not compile:

  helper/xpc_error.h:12: unknown type name 'xpc_rich_error_t'

The case itself never touches a rich error. It fails because the shared helper library it links,
libxpc_helper_tools, carries xpc_error.c, and that calls xpc_rich_error_copy_description. grep over
this library found no xpc_rich_error and no xpc_session at all: it stops at the connection API.

WHAT THIS ADDS, and it is deliberately a REAL OBJECT rather than a typedef.

  xpc_rich_error_t                    an XPC object with a description and a can-retry flag
  xpc_rich_error_copy_description()   memory the CALLER frees
  xpc_rich_error_can_retry()          a question about the error, not about the call

A typedef plus two functions would have compiled and then been wrong in a way nothing reports: the
two functions have DIFFERENT ownership rules, and copy_description handing back a pointer the caller
must free is the half that a stub gets wrong silently. copy_description answers an empty string
rather than NULL when there is nothing to say, so a caller has one shape to handle and free() is
always correct.

NOTHING IN THIS LIBRARY MAKES ONE YET, and that is the honest state. xpc_rich_error_t arrived with
xpc_session_* in macOS 12 as the replacement for reading a description out of an error dictionary.
There are no sessions here, so the only way to hold one is to be given it by a session that does not
exist. The type and its accessors are here so a caller that uses them compiles and links.

MEASURED, scripts/run-dts-batch.sh

  before  wired 67, BUILT 66, ran 66, passed 65, failed 0, did not build 1
  after   wired 67, BUILT 67, ran 67, passed 66, failed 0, did not build 0

The case does not merely build, it PASSES: connecting to a mach service that does not exist reaches
the event handler with XPC_TYPE_ERROR, which is what macOS does. The whole suite now builds and
passes, and the only line left is the case upstream never wrote a body for.
